(V1. SQL Injection in User Login) Tj
0 -14 Td
( ) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Original issue: The previous login implementation concatenated the submitted email address) Tj
0 -14 Td
(directly into the SQL statement, allowing attackers to authenticate without knowing) Tj
0 -14 Td
(passwords by injecting logical operators \(e.g., '\\' OR 1=1 --\).) Tj
0 -14 Td
( ) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Impact: Full account compromise for any registered user, enabling data exfiltration and) Tj
0 -14 Td
(fraudulent bookings.) Tj
0 -14 Td
( ) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Remediation: `login.php` now prepares the lookup query with `bind_param`, validates that the) Tj
0 -14 Td
(identifier is a well-formed email address, and blocks login for OAuth-managed accounts.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Password verification also upgrades legacy MD5 hashes to modern `password_hash` storage once) Tj
0 -14 Td
(a user successfully authenticates.) Tj
0 -14 Td
( ) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Verification: Attempting the prior payload now returns the generic login failure alert, and) Tj
0 -14 Td
(the database logs show parameterised execution without injected operators. The PHP syntax) Tj
0 -14 Td
(check \(`php -l login.php`\) passes without errors.) Tj
0 -14 Td
( ) Tj
